<title>FRANCE: Rhone-Poulenc withdraws dividend forecast.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc withdraws dividend forecast.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Rhone-Poulenc spokeswoman said a remark earlier on Thursday by company chairman Jean-Rene Fourtou about a 45 percent dividend payout in the next year was a mistake and is withdrawn.</p>
<p>She told Reuters Fourtou had meant to refer to the 1995 dividend payout ratio which was 45 percent.</p>
<p>She added the company is not making a dividend forecast.</p>
<p>Fourtou made the remark at a news conference on the French chemical company's 1996 results.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
